  <h2 id="build-it-yourself">If you build these integrations yourself</h2>
  <p>You can. Budget for the gates, not just the code. Siar's Meta review ran from 14 to {human(metaApproved).replace(/ \d{4}$/, '')} 2026, including a same-day resubmission. LinkedIn denied company-page access without a reason. TikTok's audit hasn't passed. YouTube's audit has had no answer since {human(ack).replace(/ \d{4}$/, '')}. Each network also changes its API on its own schedule; LinkedIn, for example, retires each monthly API version after about a year (see <a href="/network-changes">network API changes</a>).</p>
  <p>With Siar, your customers connect {OPEN_LIST} through apps that are live today. You get the same gates on the rest, and this page tells you where each one stands.</p>
  <HandlesBox lines={[
    'Each network\'s status, with dates. <a href="/platforms">Network status</a>',
    'Revoked or expiring connections are flagged, with a <code>social-account.updated</code> webhook. <a href="/how-publishing-works#accounts">How connections are checked</a>',
    'If a network says no, you get its own code and message, plus the fix. <a href="/how-publishing-works#errors">The network\'s own error</a>',
  ]} />

  <h2 id="price">One price for your organization, not for each account</h2>
  <p>No per-account fees. Each brand connects one account on every open network: {PLANS.STARTER.name} {PLANS.STARTER.teams} brand, {PLANS.PRO.name} {PLANS.PRO.teams}, {PLANS.BUSINESS.name} unlimited. A post sent to every connected network counts as one post.</p>
  <p>Start with {free} free posts to try. Then {prices} for one brand and {fmtInt(PLANS.STARTER.posts)} posts a month, {money('PRO', 'MONTHLY', 'usd')} ({money('PRO', 'MONTHLY', 'myr')}) for {PLANS.PRO.teams} brands and {fmtInt(PLANS.PRO.posts)} posts with a {TRIAL_DAYS}-day trial, or {money('BUSINESS', 'MONTHLY', 'usd')} ({money('BUSINESS', 'MONTHLY', 'myr')}) for unlimited brands and {fmtInt(PLANS.BUSINESS.posts)} posts. {PRICE_LOCK} <a href="/pricing">See the pricing</a>.</p>
  <p class="small muted">{LEGAL_NAME} (SSM {LEGAL_REG}), Malaysia. Meta App Review passed on {human(metaApproved)}.</p>

  <h2 id="how-kept">How this page stays true</h2>
  <p>Every row comes from Siar's own application records. When a network decides, this page, the <a href="/platforms">networks page</a> and the network's reference page read the same status, so they change in the same release, and the change goes in the <a href="/changelog">changelog</a>. A network moves to "open" only after it has approved Siar's app and a post has gone through on production.</p>
  <p>Siar publishes the refusals too, because "which networks are actually open" is the first thing you need to know, and a list that only shows wins doesn't answer it.</p>
